Hi @reporter ,

Have you tried it yet?, I have a personal project (a GUI) that starts QuestDB in process (alongside my app) on the press of a toggle button:

```java
private void onToggleQuestDB(ActionEvent ignore) {
        if (questDb == null) {
            try {
                questDb = new ServerMain("-d", Store.ROOT_PATH.getAbsolutePath());
                questDb.start(false);
                toggleQuestDB.setText("Shutdown QuestDB");
            } finally {
                results.displayMessage("QuestDB is UP");
            }
        } else {
            if (JOptionPane.YES_OPTION == JOptionPane.showConfirmDialog(
                frame,
                "Shutdown QuestDB?",
                "Choice",
                JOptionPane.YES_NO_OPTION)
            ) {
                questDb.close();
                questDb = null;
                toggleQuestDB.setText("Run QuestDB");
            }
        }
    }
```
while QuestDB is running I can go to a browser and access localhost:9000 and manage the instance like that.

